# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit gate {#the-two-qubit-gate}"
msgstr "Gate dua-qubit {#the-two-qubit-gate}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every bond $(i, j)$ of the lattice gets the same two-qubit gate, made of a Heisenberg entangler followed by random fields:\n"
msgstr "Setiap ikatan $(i, j)$ pada lattice mendapat gate dua-qubit yang sama, yang terdiri dari entangler Heisenberg diikuti medan acak:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"U_{ij} =  e^{iJ(X_iX_j + Y_iY_j + Z_iZ_j)}\\; e^{i(h_i Z_i + h_j Z_j)}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with $h$ drawn uniformly from $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ for every gate.\n"
msgstr "dengan $h$ ditarik secara seragam dari $[-\\pi/2, \\pi/2]$ untuk setiap gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** How would you decompose $U_{ij}$ into gates the hardware can run?\n"
msgstr "> **Question.** Bagaimana kamu mendekomposisi $U_{ij}$ menjadi gate yang bisa dijalankan hardware?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawaban\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The fields** are easy. $e^{ihZ}$ is a single-qubit rotation $R_Z(-2h)$ on each qubit.\n"
msgstr "**Medannya** mudah. $e^{ihZ}$ adalah rotasi satu-qubit $R_Z(-2h)$ pada setiap qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entangler** is the hard part. $XX$, $YY$ and $ZZ$ commute, so it factors into three rotations, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ and $R_{ZZ}$. Each takes two CNOTs, which makes six CNOTs per gate.\n"
msgstr "**Entangler-nya** bagian yang sulit. $XX$, $YY$ dan $ZZ$ saling komut, jadi bisa difaktorkan menjadi tiga rotasi, $R_{XX}$, $R_{YY}$ dan $R_{ZZ}$. Masing-masing butuh dua CNOT, sehingga totalnya enam CNOT per gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is a better way. Any two-qubit gate can be built from at most three CNOTs and single-qubit rotations. The optimal circuit starts from the form $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, and this entangler already has that form with $a = b = c = J$. So it maps straight onto three CNOTs, and the single-qubit angles are linear in $J$. The experiment code builds the gate this way.\n"
msgstr "Ada cara yang lebih baik. Gate dua-qubit apa pun bisa dibangun dari paling banyak tiga CNOT dan rotasi satu-qubit. Circuit optimalnya dimulai dari bentuk $e^{i(aXX + bYY + cZZ)}$, dan entangler ini sudah punya bentuk itu dengan $a = b = c = J$. Jadi ia langsung dipetakan ke tiga CNOT, dan sudut satu-qubit-nya linear terhadap $J$. Kode eksperimen membangun gate dengan cara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On hardware, every two-qubit gate adds noise, so halving the CNOT count matters.\n"
msgstr "Di hardware, setiap gate dua-qubit menambah noise, jadi menghemat separuh jumlah CNOT itu penting.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

