# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The brickwork and the Floquet cycle {#the-brickwork-and-the-floquet-cycle}"
msgstr "Brickwork dan siklus Floquet {#the-brickwork-and-the-floquet-cycle}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The gates tile the square lattice in four *sublayers* of non-overlapping bonds, a brickwork: horizontal bonds starting on even columns, then odd columns, then vertical bonds starting on even rows, then odd rows. Qubit $y \\cdot L_x + x$ sits at site $(x, y)$.\n"
msgstr "Gate-gate menutupi lattice persegi dalam empat *sublayer* ikatan yang tidak tumpang tindih, sebuah brickwork: ikatan horizontal mulai dari kolom genap, lalu kolom ganjil, lalu ikatan vertikal mulai dari baris genap, lalu baris ganjil. Qubit $y \\cdot L_x + x$ berada di situs $(x, y)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The four sublayers make one *Floquet cycle*. The cycle repeats $n_F$ times with **the same fields**, so the dynamics are random in space and periodic in time. The circuit starts from the Néel state, and $n_F$ is half the side length of the lattice.\n"
"The next cell draws one Floquet cycle of the $8 \\times 8$ hardware lattice, sublayer by sublayer, with the fields of the hardware run, in the style of Figure 5 of the paper. Thick bonds are the gates of each sublayer. Each qubit a gate acts on is colored by the random field $h$ it then receives, and idle qubits are white. The arrows show the Néel initial state, with $\\uparrow$ for $|0\\rangle$. The paper's figure applies the vertical sublayers first; neither order is expected to change the physics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keempat sublayer membentuk satu *siklus Floquet*. Siklus ini berulang $n_F$ kali dengan **medan yang sama**, jadi dinamikanya acak dalam ruang dan periodik dalam waktu. Circuit dimulai dari state Néel, dan $n_F$ adalah setengah panjang sisi lattice.\n"
"Cell berikut menggambar satu siklus Floquet dari lattice hardware $8 \\times 8$, sublayer demi sublayer, dengan medan dari run hardware, dalam gaya Gambar 5 di makalah. Ikatan tebal adalah gate dari setiap sublayer. Setiap qubit yang dikenai gate diwarnai sesuai medan acak $h$ yang kemudian diterimanya, dan qubit yang menganggur berwarna putih. Panah menunjukkan state awal Néel, dengan $\\uparrow$ untuk $|0\\rangle$. Gambar di makalah menerapkan sublayer vertikal lebih dulu; urutan mana pun tidak diperkirakan mengubah fisikanya.\n"

