msgid "3. Noise, and how to undo it {#3-noise-and-how-to-undo-it}"
msgstr "3. Noise, dan cara menghilangkannya {#3-noise-and-how-to-undo-it}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A noisy simulation {#a-noisy-simulation}"
msgstr "Simulasi dengan noise {#a-noisy-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now add noise: 1% two-qubit depolarizing noise on every CZ gate and a 3% readout error on every qubit, sampled with the Qiskit Aer sampler. With 144 CZ gates in the circuit, this is much less noise than the 8×8 hardware circuits see, but enough to see what it does. The simulation uses six couplings and 4,000 shots each, and takes about 1.5 minutes.\n"
"> **Question.** Before you run it: will noise make the system look more thermalized or less thermalized?\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang tambahkan noise: noise depolarizing dua-qubit 1% pada setiap gate CZ dan error readout 3% pada setiap qubit, disampel dengan Sampler Qiskit Aer. Dengan 144 gate CZ di circuit, noise ini jauh lebih kecil daripada yang dialami circuit hardware 8×8, tetapi cukup untuk melihat efeknya. Simulasi memakai enam coupling dan masing-masing 4.000 shot, dan butuh sekitar 1,5 menit.\n"
"> **Pertanyaan.** Sebelum kamu menjalankannya: apakah noise membuat sistem terlihat lebih terthermalisasi atau kurang terthermalisasi?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More. Noise scrambles the outcomes, which pushes every marginal distribution toward uniform, so the raw IPR drops and the entropy rises. Without mitigation, noise looks like thermalization that is not there, and the crossovers come out too early.\n"
msgstr "Lebih. Noise mengacak hasil, sehingga setiap distribusi marginal terdorong ke arah seragam, jadi IPR mentah turun dan entropi naik. Tanpa mitigasi, noise terlihat seperti thermalisasi yang sebenarnya tidak ada, dan crossover muncul terlalu awal.\n"

