msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/8680e8eb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Brainstorm: how would you undo this? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"
msgstr "Brainstorm: bagaimana cara menghilangkannya? {#brainstorm-how-would-you-undo-this}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Suggested approach\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Pendekatan yang disarankan\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At small $J$, the state is barely entangled, so the ideal answer there is cheap to compute classically, even for 64 qubits. That suggests measuring the effect of the noise at a small calibration coupling $J_0$ and correcting every other coupling with it. There are two natural ways to do that, called low-entanglement calibration (LEC):\n"
msgstr "Pada $J$ kecil, state hampir tidak terentangle, jadi jawaban idealnya murah dihitung secara klasik, bahkan untuk 64 qubit. Ini menyarankan kita mengukur efek noise pada coupling kalibrasi kecil $J_0$ dan mengoreksi semua coupling lain dengannya. Ada dua cara yang wajar untuk melakukannya, disebut low-entanglement calibration (LEC):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the IPR.** Rescale the excess of the IPR over its value for a uniform distribution, $2^{-n_A}$, by one factor per marginal:\n"
msgstr "**LEC pada IPR.** Skalakan kelebihan IPR di atas nilainya untuk distribusi seragam, $2^{-n_A}$, dengan satu faktor per marginal:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A} + R_0\\bigl(\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J) - 2^{-n_A}\\bigr), \\qquad R_0 = \\frac{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{ideal}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}{\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{raw}}_A(J_0) - 2^{-n_A}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**LEC on the $\\langle Z \\rangle$ expectation values.** Rescale every parity of the marginal by its own factor, and rebuild the IPR with the Parseval formula:\n"
msgstr "**LEC pada nilai ekspektasi $\\langle Z \\rangle$.** Skalakan setiap paritas dari marginal dengan faktornya sendiri, lalu bangun kembali IPR dengan rumus Parseval:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Large\n"
"r_S = \\frac{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{ideal}}(J_0)}{\\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J_0)}, \\qquad\n"
"\\mathrm{IPR}^{\\mathrm{LEC}}_A(J) = 2^{-n_A}\\Bigl(1 + \\sum_{S} r_S^2 \\, \\langle Z_S \\rangle^{\\mathrm{raw}}(J)^2\\Bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the code, each squared rescaled parity is debiased by subtracting its variance, as in section 2.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kode, setiap paritas terskala yang dikuadratkan di-debias dengan mengurangi variansnya, seperti di bagian 2.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are the same if every $r_S^2$ equals $R_0$.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya sama jika setiap $r_S^2$ sama dengan $R_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"> **Question.** What are the pros and cons of these methods?\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Pros**\n"
msgstr "**Pros**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cheap:** no extra data is needed from the device, only a classical simulation at $J_0$.\n"
msgstr "**Murah:** tidak butuh data tambahan dari device, hanya simulasi klasik pada $J_0$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Uses the structure of the circuit:** the circuit depth and the CZ layers do not change with $J$, so the noise at $J_0$ is the same noise as at every other $J$.\n"
msgstr "**Memakai struktur circuit:** kedalaman circuit dan layer CZ tidak berubah terhadap $J$, jadi noise pada $J_0$ sama dengan noise pada setiap $J$ lainnya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cons**\n"
msgstr "**Cons**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assumes the effect of the noise on the observables does not depend on $J$:** the noise itself is the same, but how it damps the IPR or each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ can change as $J$ grows.\n"
msgstr "**Mengasumsikan efek noise pada observable tidak bergantung pada $J$:** noisenya sendiri sama, tetapi cara noise meredam IPR atau tiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ bisa berubah saat $J$ membesar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods on the noisy simulation {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"
msgstr "Kedua metode pada simulasi dengan noise {#both-methods-on-the-noisy-simulation}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/212cb53d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both methods remove most of the damage: the raw estimates in the previous plot are far too random, and the mitigated ones follow the exact curves. The differences show up for the larger marginals.\n"
msgstr "Kedua metode menghilangkan sebagian besar kerusakan: estimasi mentah di plot sebelumnya terlalu acak, dan estimasi yang sudah dimitigasi mengikuti kurva eksak. Perbedaannya terlihat pada marginal yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the small marginals both methods work. For the $3 \\times 3$ marginal, LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ is clearly closer.\n"
msgstr "Untuk marginal kecil, kedua metode berhasil. Untuk marginal $3 \\times 3$, LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ jelas lebih dekat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on the IPR gives too little entropy.** Too little entropy means the IPR is too big: LEC on the IPR over-inflates it. It assumes that noise damps the contribution of every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ to the IPR by the same factor. At $J_0$, every $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ is close to $\\pm 1$, so all strings contribute equally, and most strings have medium weight: of the 511 strings of a $3 \\times 3$ marginal, 252 have weight 4 or 5, and only nine have weight 1. Noise damps a string more the higher its weight (readout error alone damps a weight-$w$ string by $0.94^w$), so the single factor $R_0$ is set mainly by the damping of medium-weight strings. As $J$ grows, the higher-weight $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ decay fastest, and the IPR is carried more and more by low-weight strings, which noise damps less. Boosting them with a factor learned mainly from more heavily damped strings over-inflates the IPR. The effect grows with the size of the marginal, since a larger marginal has a wider range of weights. It is largest at intermediate $J$, after the mix of strings has shifted but while the excess of the IPR over its uniform value still matters.\n"
msgstr "**Mengapa LEC pada IPR menghasilkan entropi terlalu kecil.** Entropi terlalu kecil berarti IPR terlalu besar: LEC pada IPR menggelembungkannya berlebihan. Metode ini mengasumsikan bahwa noise meredam kontribusi setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ ke IPR dengan faktor yang sama. Pada $J_0$, setiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ mendekati $\\pm 1$, jadi semua string berkontribusi sama, dan kebanyakan string punya bobot sedang: dari 511 string marginal $3 \\times 3$, 252 punya bobot 4 atau 5, dan hanya sembilan yang berbobot 1. Noise meredam string makin kuat jika bobotnya makin tinggi (error readout saja meredam string berbobot-$w$ sebesar $0.94^w$), jadi faktor tunggal $R_0$ terutama ditentukan oleh peredaman string berbobot sedang. Saat $J$ membesar, $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ berbobot lebih tinggi meluruh paling cepat, dan IPR makin banyak dibawa oleh string berbobot rendah, yang diredam noise lebih sedikit. Mengangkat string-string itu dengan faktor yang dipelajari terutama dari string yang lebih kuat teredam akan menggelembungkan IPR berlebihan. Efeknya tumbuh seiring ukuran marginal, karena marginal yang lebih besar punya rentang bobot lebih lebar. Efeknya terbesar pada $J$ menengah, setelah campuran string bergeser tetapi selagi kelebihan IPR di atas nilai serAGAMnya masih berarti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ errs the other way.** It rescales each string by its own factor, so the shift between weights does not affect it. It only assumes that each string keeps its $J_0$ damping. As $J$ grows, each $Z_S$ spreads into higher-weight operators, which pick up more noise than at $J_0$, so the factors slightly under-correct and the entropy comes out slightly too high.\n"
msgstr "**Mengapa LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ salah ke arah sebaliknya.** Metode ini menskalakan tiap string dengan faktornya sendiri, jadi pergeseran antar bobot tidak memengaruhinya. Ia hanya mengasumsikan bahwa tiap string mempertahankan peredamannya pada $J_0$. Saat $J$ membesar, tiap $Z_S$ menyebar ke operator berbobot lebih tinggi, yang menerima lebih banyak noise daripada pada $J_0$, sehingga faktornya sedikit kurang mengoreksi dan entropi keluar sedikit terlalu tinggi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the prediction to test on hardware is: **the larger the marginal, the more LEC on $\\langle Z \\rangle$ should win**. On hardware, the noise is stronger and not of a known form.\n"
msgstr "Jadi prediksi yang perlu diuji di hardware adalah: **makin besar marginal, makin besar kemungkinan LEC pada $\\langle Z \\rangle$ menang**. Di hardware, noise lebih kuat dan tidak berbentuk yang dikenal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Run at scale {#4-run-at-scale}"
msgstr "4. Jalankan dalam skala besar {#4-run-at-scale}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware experiment runs an $8 \\times 8$ lattice with four cycles: 64 qubits and 1,344 CZ gates in 48 layers, at nine couplings. Five things change compared with the simulation:\n"
msgstr "Eksperimen hardware menjalankan lattice $8 \\times 8$ dengan empat siklus: 64 qubit dan 1.344 gate CZ dalam 48 layer, pada sembilan coupling. Lima hal berubah dibandingkan simulasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The noise has to be **learned**, which only works if the CZ layers are fixed.\n"
msgstr "Noise harus **dipelajari**, yang hanya berhasil jika layer CZ-nya tetap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Twirling** turns the noise of each layer into a Pauli channel, which can be learned and amplified.\n"
msgstr "**Twirling** mengubah noise tiap layer menjadi channel Pauli, yang bisa dipelajari dan diamplifikasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dynamical decoupling (DD)** protects idle qubits.\n"
msgstr "**Dynamical decoupling (DD)** melindungi qubit yang menganggur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Noise amplification** for PEA runs in the same job as the main data.\n"
msgstr "**Amplifikasi noise** untuk PEA berjalan dalam job yang sama dengan data utama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**MPS simulations** at small $J$ provide the classical references for LEC-based error mitigation.\n"
msgstr "**Simulasi MPS** pada $J$ kecil menyediakan referensi klasik untuk mitigasi error berbasis LEC.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cells that need a backend only run when `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` is `True`. MPS simulations can be rerun with `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` set to `True`. The other cells run here.\n"
msgstr "Cell yang butuh backend hanya berjalan saat `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` bernilai `True`. Simulasi MPS bisa dijalankan ulang dengan `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` diatur ke `True`. Cell lainnya berjalan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixed CZ layers {#fixed-cz-layers}"
msgstr "Layer CZ tetap {#fixed-cz-layers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Boxes for noise learning {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"
msgstr "Box untuk noise learning {#boxes-for-noise-learning}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Samplomatic boxing pass manager then groups each circuit into *boxes*: one per CZ layer and one for the measurements. Each box carries a reference to the noise model it needs, so you can check that all couplings share the same boxes. The next cell does this for the $8 \\times 8$ circuits of the hardware run, compiled to CZ gates without a backend, and prints the boxes that noise learning will characterize.\n"
msgstr "Pass manager boxing Samplomatic lalu mengelompokkan setiap circuit menjadi *box*: satu per layer CZ dan satu untuk pengukuran. Setiap box membawa referensi ke model noise yang dibutuhkannya, jadi kamu bisa memeriksa bahwa semua coupling memakai box yang sama. Cell berikutnya melakukan ini untuk circuit $8 \\times 8$ dari run hardware, dikompilasi ke gate CZ tanpa backend, dan mencetak box yang akan dikarakterisasi oleh noise learning.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirl the circuits {#twirl-the-circuits}"
msgstr "Twirl circuit {#twirl-the-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In every randomization, Samplomatic puts random Pauli gates before each box and the compensating gates after it, merged into the neighboring single-qubit gates. Averaged over randomizations, the noise of each layer becomes a Pauli channel, which `NoiseLearnerV3` can learn as a sparse Pauli-Lindblad model and the PEA step can amplify. Measurement twirling randomly flips bits before readout. The flips are undone in software, which makes the readout noise symmetric and is the basis of the readout correction (TREX).\n"
msgstr "Dalam setiap randomisasi, Samplomatic menaruh gate Pauli acak sebelum tiap box dan gate kompensasi setelahnya, digabung ke gate satu-qubit di sekitarnya. Dirata-rata atas randomisasi, noise tiap layer menjadi channel Pauli, yang bisa dipelajari `NoiseLearnerV3` sebagai model Pauli-Lindblad yang jarang (sparse) dan bisa diamplifikasi oleh langkah PEA. Twirling pengukuran membalik bit secara acak sebelum readout. Pembalikan itu dibatalkan di software, yang membuat noise readout simetris dan menjadi dasar koreksi readout (TREX).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware workflow {#the-hardware-workflow}"
msgstr "Alur kerja hardware {#the-hardware-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the qubits, compile the circuits, then learn the noise and run the sweep. These cells are switched off here.\n"
msgstr "Pilih qubit, kompilasi circuit, lalu pelajari noise dan jalankan sweep. Cell-cell ini dimatikan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose the qubits.** Nighthawk's square grid holds the $8 \\times 8$ lattice without SWAP gates. The cell scores every $8 \\times 8$ rectangle of the grid by its reported CZ and readout errors and takes the best.\n"
msgstr "**Pilih qubit.** Grid persegi Nighthawk memuat lattice $8 \\times 8$ tanpa gate SWAP. Cell ini memberi skor setiap persegi panjang $8 \\times 8$ di grid berdasarkan error CZ dan readout yang dilaporkan, lalu mengambil yang terbaik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Compile.** The same steps as above on the chosen qubits, followed by `build`, which turns each boxed circuit into a template circuit and a *samplex*, the recipe for drawing the twirling gates and the injected noise. DD is added to the templates.\n"
msgstr "**Kompilasi.** Langkah yang sama seperti di atas pada qubit terpilih, diikuti `build`, yang mengubah tiap circuit ber-box menjadi circuit template dan sebuah *samplex*, resep untuk menarik gate twirling dan noise yang disuntikkan. DD ditambahkan ke template.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Learn the noise and run the sweep.** One `NoiseLearnerV3` job learns all five boxes: a Pauli-Lindblad model for each of the four CZ layers, and the readout noise of the measurement box. Then one `QuantumProgram` holds all nine couplings. Each item gets its template, its samplex, the learned noise models, and three noise scales. A scale of 0 is the unamplified data for both LEC methods. Scales of 0.5 and 1 add 50% and 100% of the learned noise for PEA, which extrapolates back to zero noise. This uses about 40 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "**Pelajari noise dan jalankan sweep.** Satu job `NoiseLearnerV3` mempelajari kelima box: model Pauli-Lindblad untuk tiap dari empat layer CZ, dan noise readout dari box pengukuran. Lalu satu `QuantumProgram` memuat kesembilan coupling. Tiap item mendapat template-nya, samplex-nya, model noise yang dipelajari, dan tiga skala noise. Skala 0 adalah data tanpa amplifikasi untuk kedua metode LEC. Skala 0,5 dan 1 menambah 50% dan 100% noise yang dipelajari untuk PEA, yang mengekstrapolasi kembali ke noise nol. Ini memakai sekitar 40 detik waktu QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. The hardware data {#5-the-hardware-data}"
msgstr "5. Data hardware {#5-the-hardware-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section explores how the previous methods perform on real hardware data from a Nighthawk processor.\n"
msgstr "Bagian ini mengeksplorasi bagaimana metode-metode sebelumnya bekerja pada data hardware nyata dari prosesor Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the run {#load-the-run}"
msgstr "Muat run {#load-the-run}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` set to `True`, the next cell converts the results of the two jobs from section 4 and saves them to `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, in the same format as the saved run, so the new run can be analyzed again later. Otherwise it loads the saved run from `data/hardware_run.npz`. The bits are packed along the qubit axis to save space.\n"
msgstr "Dengan `RUN_ON_HARDWARE` diatur ke `True`, cell berikutnya mengonversi hasil kedua job dari bagian 4 dan menyimpannya ke `data/hardware_run_new.npz`, dalam format yang sama dengan run yang tersimpan, sehingga run baru bisa dianalisis lagi nanti. Jika tidak, cell ini memuat run tersimpan dari `data/hardware_run.npz`. Bit dikemas sepanjang sumbu qubit untuk menghemat ruang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the kernel restarts while the jobs run, do not submit them again. Rerun the cells before the last call in section 4, check that the same qubits are chosen, and set `learner_job` and `executor_job` to `service.job(job_id)` with the job IDs that were printed out in section 4.\n"
msgstr "Jika kernel restart saat job berjalan, jangan kirim ulang job-nya. Jalankan ulang cell sebelum panggilan terakhir di bagian 4, periksa bahwa qubit yang sama dipilih, lalu atur `learner_job` dan `executor_job` ke `service.job(job_id)` dengan ID job yang dicetak di bagian 4.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical references {#classical-references}"
msgstr "Referensi klasik {#classical-references}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both LEC methods need the ideal marginal distributions at $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, and testing them needs ideal values at the held-out couplings $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$. These come from matrix product state (MPS) simulations, saved for every placement of each marginal shape on the lattice, as in the paper, and for every non-overlapping $2 \\times 2$ block at $J_0$. At $J_0$ they converge at bond dimension $\\chi = 64$. At $J = 0.01\\pi$ and $0.02\\pi$ they use $\\chi = 128$, and at $0.02\\pi$ they still change by up to about 13% from $\\chi = 64$ for $3 \\times 3$ marginals, so treat them as approximate there. The next cell computes them if `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` is `True`, which takes about 18 minutes, and otherwise loads the saved results, keyed by coupling index, bond dimension, and marginal.\n"
msgstr "Kedua metode LEC butuh distribusi marginal ideal pada $J_0 = 0.005\\pi$, dan untuk mengujinya dibutuhkan nilai ideal pada coupling held-out $J = 0.01\\pi$ dan $0.02\\pi$. Nilai-nilai ini berasal dari simulasi matrix product state (MPS), disimpan untuk setiap penempatan tiap bentuk marginal di lattice, seperti di paper, dan untuk setiap blok $2 \\times 2$ yang tidak tumpang tindih pada $J_0$. Pada $J_0$ simulasi konvergen pada bond dimension $\\chi = 64$. Pada $J = 0.01\\pi$ dan $0.02\\pi$ dipakai $\\chi = 128$, dan pada $0.02\\pi$ nilainya masih berubah hingga sekitar 13% dari $\\chi = 64$ untuk marginal $3 \\times 3$, jadi anggap sebagai perkiraan di sana. Cell berikutnya menghitungnya jika `COMPUTE_MPS_REFERENCES` bernilai `True`, yang butuh sekitar 18 menit, dan jika tidak, memuat hasil tersimpan, dengan kunci berupa indeks coupling, bond dimension, dan marginal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data quality: faulty couplers / qubits {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"
msgstr "Kualitas data: coupler / qubit yang rusak {#data-quality-faulty-couplers--qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, look at the lowest coupling, $J_0$, where the expectation values should be close to the Néel checkerboard.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, lihat coupling terendah, $J_0$, di mana nilai ekspektasi seharusnya mendekati checkerboard Néel.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/48d2dbbb-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Question.** Looking at the hardware map, what stands out?\n"
msgstr "> **Pertanyaan.** Melihat peta hardware, apa yang menonjol?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The pale sites, which have lost almost all of their signal although the state at $J_0$ is close to the Néel state. They matter because LEC divides by whatever signal survives at $J_0$: a qubit with almost no signal gives a huge, noisy correction factor, and a few such qubits can dominate every marginal that contains them.\n"
msgstr "Site yang pucat, yang kehilangan hampir seluruh sinyalnya padahal state pada $J_0$ mendekati state Néel. Site ini penting karena LEC membagi dengan sinyal apa pun yang tersisa pada $J_0$: qubit dengan sinyal nyaris nol memberi faktor koreksi yang sangat besar dan berisik, dan beberapa qubit seperti itu bisa mendominasi setiap marginal yang memuatnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A rule that uses only the data: A qubit is faulty if its single-qubit IPR at $J_0$ is within $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ of $1/2$, the value for a fully mixed qubit. Since the IPR of one qubit is $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, this flags qubits with $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Marginals that contain a flagged site are left out below.\n"
msgstr "Aturan yang hanya memakai data: sebuah qubit rusak jika IPR satu-qubitnya pada $J_0$ berada dalam $0.25^2/2 \\approx 0.03$ dari $1/2$, nilai untuk qubit yang sepenuhnya tercampur. Karena IPR satu qubit adalah $(1 + \\langle Z \\rangle^2)/2$, ini menandai qubit dengan $|\\langle Z \\rangle| < 0.25$. Marginal yang memuat site yang ditandai dikeluarkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Select the marginals to average {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"
msgstr "Pilih marginal untuk dirata-rata {#select-the-marginals-to-average}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next cell shows which placements of each shape enter the averages below: every placement in the bulk of the lattice without a flagged site (red crosses). Placements that touch the edge (shaded) are left out. Edge qubits have fewer bonds, so they scramble more slowly. Averaged on their own, they cross over a full step of $J$ later than bulk placements, for every shape and method. Each averaged placement has its own box, colored by placement.\n"
msgstr "Cell berikutnya menunjukkan penempatan tiap bentuk yang masuk ke rata-rata di bawah: setiap penempatan di bagian bulk lattice tanpa site yang ditandai (tanda silang merah). Penempatan yang menyentuh tepi (diarsir) dikeluarkan. Qubit tepi punya lebih sedikit bond, jadi mengacak lebih lambat. Jika dirata-rata sendiri, mereka melakukan crossover satu langkah penuh $J$ lebih lambat daripada penempatan bulk, untuk setiap bentuk dan metode. Setiap penempatan yang dirata-rata punya box-nya sendiri, diberi warna menurut penempatan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/d31b217b-0.avif)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA {#pea}"
msgstr "PEA {#pea}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The third method needs no classical reference. For each parity, take the values at noise factors 1, 1.5, and 2, divide out the learned readout damping (TREX), fit an exponential in the noise factor, and extrapolate to zero noise. Parities that change sign or are nearly zero get a straight-line fit. Subtracting the variance needs a reliable estimate of it, which is easy for raw and rescaled parities but not for the output of a nonlinear fit with clipping and fallbacks. PEA therefore uses the other standard way to remove the bias of a square. Extrapolate each half of the randomizations separately and multiply the two independent estimates.\n"
msgstr "Metode ketiga tidak butuh referensi klasik. Untuk setiap paritas, ambil nilai pada faktor noise 1, 1,5, dan 2, bagi dengan peredaman readout yang dipelajari (TREX), fit eksponensial terhadap faktor noise, dan ekstrapolasi ke noise nol. Paritas yang berganti tanda atau hampir nol memakai fit garis lurus. Mengurangi varians butuh estimasi varians yang andal, yang mudah untuk paritas mentah dan terskala tetapi tidak untuk keluaran fit nonlinear dengan clipping dan fallback. Karena itu PEA memakai cara standar lain untuk menghilangkan bias kuadrat. Ekstrapolasikan tiap separuh randomisasi secara terpisah dan kalikan kedua estimasi independen itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "All four estimates, and the crossovers {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"
msgstr "Keempat estimasi, dan crossover-nya {#all-four-estimates-and-the-crossovers}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next function computes the raw, LEC-on-IPR, LEC-on-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, and PEA estimates of the IPR of one marginal position at every coupling. It also estimates the shot noise of each, by bootstrapping the randomizations. The cell runs it for every placement that enters the averages, which takes about a minute and a half.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi berikutnya menghitung estimasi mentah, LEC-pada-IPR, LEC-pada-$\\langle Z \\rangle$, dan PEA dari IPR satu posisi marginal pada setiap coupling. Fungsi ini juga mengestimasi shot noise masing-masing, dengan bootstrapping atas randomisasi. Cell menjalankannya untuk setiap penempatan yang masuk ke rata-rata, yang butuh sekitar satu setengah menit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/onset-of-ergodicity/extracted-outputs/6303dec9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wrap-up {#wrap-up}"
msgstr "Penutup {#wrap-up}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What it took to run an experiment of this size:\n"
msgstr "Yang dibutuhkan untuk menjalankan eksperimen sebesar ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuits whose structure does not depend on $J$**, compiled one sublayer at a time, so one noise model serves the whole sweep.\n"
msgstr "**Circuit yang strukturnya tidak bergantung pada $J$**, dikompilasi satu sublayer pada satu waktu, sehingga satu model noise melayani seluruh sweep.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Estimators that work from bitstrings**: pair counting for the IPR of a marginal, and the Parseval form, with the variance subtracted from each squared parity, when the inputs are mitigated expectation values.\n"
msgstr "**Estimator yang bekerja dari bitstring**: penghitungan pasangan untuk IPR sebuah marginal, dan bentuk Parseval, dengan varians dikurangkan dari tiap paritas kuadrat, ketika inputnya adalah nilai ekspektasi yang sudah dimitigasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**A cheap classical anchor**: the ideal state at small $J$ calibrates the noise, and held-out couplings test the calibration. Calibrating each $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ separately, rather than the IPR as a whole, is what makes the large marginals agree.\n"
msgstr "**Jangkar klasik yang murah**: state ideal pada $J$ kecil mengalibrasi noise, dan coupling held-out menguji kalibrasinya. Mengalibrasi tiap $\\langle Z_S \\rangle$ secara terpisah, bukan IPR secara keseluruhan, adalah yang membuat marginal besar cocok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**IBM tools for the heavy lifting**: Samplomatic boxes and twirling, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, and one `Executor` job with noise amplification for PEA.\n"
msgstr "**Tool IBM untuk pekerjaan berat**: box dan twirling Samplomatic, `NoiseLearnerV3`, dynamical decoupling, dan satu job `Executor` dengan amplifikasi noise untuk PEA.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Data-quality checks** that use only the data.\n"
msgstr "**Pemeriksaan kualitas data** yang hanya memakai data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Next steps.** To go further with mitigation, see the [probabilistic error amplification](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) and [PEC with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) tutorials.\n"
msgstr "**Langkah berikutnya.** Untuk mendalami mitigasi, lihat tutorial [probabilistic error amplification](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-amplification) dan [PEC with shaded lightcones](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones).\n"

